From 2f13b5b6324a7c8990cc399677d8d449cc7e6387 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qr0n <77075118+qr0n@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 17:32:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CUDA: internal AllReduce for N GPUs, not just 2

The internal AllReduce refused anything but two devices, so -sm tensor on
three or more GPUs fell back to the meta backend's f32-through-host exchange.

Chunked kernel: signal once, wait on every peer's arrival slot, then sum all
N contributions. Copy-engine path: dev_tmp holds N-1 peer slices, stage 1
waits for every peer to finish reading our host_large, and the add kernel
sums every slice. Every GPU sums in rank order so results stay bit-identical
across GPUs; for N == 2 this is the same arithmetic as before. The two-GPU
chunked kernel is a separate instantiation with N fixed at compile time.

Validated with GGML_CUDA_DEVICES virtual devices on 2x P100, Llama-3.1-8B
Q4_K_M, 20-chunk perplexity:
  2 devices: 10.2602 / 10.2652 (bf16 on/off), identical to 190fae9
  3 devices: 10.2585 with bf16 off on chunked-only, copy-engine-only and
             mixed paths (stock fallback: 10.2568)
  4 devices: 10.2705, identical to the stock fallback
2-card tg128 unchanged (80.0 vs 79.8). No speed data for real 3+ GPU systems.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
